1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,720
In this tutorial, you'll learn how to intercept requests with burp proxy.

2
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:16,880
Burp proxy lets you intercept HTTP requests and responses sent between burp's browser and the

3
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:22,960
target server. This enables you to study how a website behaves when you perform different actions.

4
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:31,960
Go to the proxy intercept tab. Click the intercept is off button so that it toggles to intercept is on.

5
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:39,940
Click open browser. This launches burp's browser which is pre-configured to work with burp right out

6
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:45,220
of the box. Position the windows so that you can see both burp and burp's browser.

7
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:55,000
Using the browser, try to visit portswigger.net and observe that the site doesn't load.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,060
Burp proxy has intercepted the HTTP request that was issued by the browser before it could reach

9
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:08,080
the server. You can see this intercept request on the proxy intercept tab. The request is held here

10
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:15,160
so that you can study it and even modify it before forwarding to the target server. Click the forward

11
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:20,560
button several times to send the intercept request and any subsequent ones until the page loads in

12
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:27,040
burp's browser. Due to the number of requests browsers typically send, you often won't want to intercept

13
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:33,160
every single one of them. Click the intercept is on button so that it now says intercept is off.

14
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:44,080
Go back to the browser and confirm that you can interact with the site as normal. In burp, go to the proxy HTTP

15
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:52,180
history tab. Here you can see the history of all HTTP traffic that has passed through burp proxy, even when

16
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:59,080
interception was switched off. Click on any entry in the history to view the raw HTTP request along with

17
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:05,440
the corresponding response from the server. This lets you explore the website as normal and study the

18
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:10,320
interactions between burp's browser and the server afterward, which is more convenient in many cases.

